From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] windows.media.speech: The WinRT synthesizer speaks (6510)

SpeechSynthesizer had no voices and its streams were empty objects.
The installed voices are now SAPI's voice tokens (AllVoices,
DefaultVoice, a new synthesizer's voice), and the voice's engine
(msttsengine's eSpeak NG voice) speaks the text, or the SSML read
down to its text and breaks, into a RIFF/WAVE stream. The stream
answers as IRandomAccessStream, IInputStream, IOutputStream,
IClosable and IContentTypeProvider ("audio/wav") over
windows.storage's stream, and carries SpeechWord and SpeechSentence
markers when the options ask for them. SpeakingRate, AudioVolume and
AudioPitch apply; text that is not SSML fails the operation with the
format error. The engine side lives apart (sapi_engine.c) since
sapi.h and the WinRT speech headers name the same interfaces.
